de and the Primodial War were both &quot;Humanity is out numbered, out gunned, by hostile and alien powers.&quot; And in both cases, yeah, the exalted adapted and won. :monty python yay:<br /> <br /> My other thought is I think an alien invasion by a Weyland-Yutani corp is...less interesting then alien invasions could be? I feel like an alien invasion in Exalted would be more interesting if we removed the assumption that there aren't...alien exalted. Hell, dig up Gunstar Autobot and find those knock off lunars and sids hinted there plus some other stuff. I'm thinking of say, Dragonball, where the aliens have technology and such, but they also use the same general martial arts-supernatural rules as everyone else did on 'Earth'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T03:12:10-07:00","id":1297673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297140-exalted-meeting-alien-invasion?p=1297671#post1297671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My other thought is I think an alien invasion by a Weyland-Yutani corp is...less interesting then alien invasions could be? I feel like an alien invasion in Exalted would be more interesting if we removed the assumption that there aren't...alien exalted. Hell, dig up Gunstar Autobot and find those knock off lunars and sids hinted there plus some other stuff. I'm thinking of say, Dragonball, where the aliens have technology and such, but they also use the same general martial arts-supernatural rules as everyone else did on 'Earth'</div> </div> </div> </div>Autochthonia and its inhabitants were initially conceived as an &quot;alien invaders&quot; type of scenario, except the &quot;aliens&quot; came from another dimension rather than another planet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T03:29:57-07:00","id":1297676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297140-exalted-meeting-alien-invasion?p=1297673#post1297673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Autochthonia and its inhabitants were initially conceived as an &quot;alien invaders&quot; type of scenario, except the &quot;aliens&quot; came from another dimension rather than another planet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now we need a nanoha crossover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-22T21:59:44-07:00","id":1298847,"title":"","content":"You missed the part of Part 2 where you find out your commanding officer\u2019s been a Lunar since halfway through Part 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T15:57:13-07:00","id":1299062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297140-exalted-meeting-alien-invasion?p=1297633#post1297633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any examples?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really - it's not really the sort of thing I archive, or would have an easy time finding through keyword searchs, plus we've gone through at least one wholesale loss of forum conversations since much of it would've taken place. It's entirely possible, I may be exaggerating through a sort of false memory unreliable syndrome writ small, to boot! (Also, to clarify, fully hyperbole, certainly not actually traumatic or stressful, though thanks for the concern guys).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297140-exalted-meeting-alien-invasion?p=1297671#post1297671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My other thought is I think an alien invasion by a Weyland-Yutani corp is...less interesting then alien invasions could be? I feel like an alien invasion in Exalted would be more interesting if we removed the assumption that there aren't...alien exalted. Hell, dig up Gunstar Autobot and find those knock off lunars and sids hinted there plus some other stuff. I'm thinking of say, Dragonball, where the aliens have technology and such, but they also use the same general martial arts-supernatural rules as everyone else did on 'Earth'</div> </div> </div> </div>Being in a more sympathetic frame of mind, maybe I think there's some room for fun, particularly if you play up The Corp as kinda like The Guild in flatworld Exalted; they've encountered strongly powered aliens before (if not in the shape of heroes of myth, exactly!) and have an institutional structure and savvy that's at least somewhat prepared to deal with excession type threats. A little different to OP scenario. Of course, there's a fine line there to dealing with a version of the dissatisfactions that crop up when The Guild is portrayed as uber-competent against the Exalted.<br /> <br /> (Reading OP again, why is this not-exactly-Creation planet of Exalted not already a galatic power before Alien-Evil-Corp turns up as well?).<br /> <br /> (Though yeah, perhaps there is more fun in supertech aliens who play in something resembling a heroic action genre on the level of the Exalted though - Vash, Alita and Lord Boros vs the Exalted, sort of thing?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T02:14:40-07:00","id":1323397,"title":"","content":"*thinks* <br /> <br /> So I've been wondering. Again. About things. Sorry if this gets repetitive, but I need some place to put my thoughts. <br /> <br /> <br /> Let's punt an Exaltation into Eclipse phase. Probably..... a Jovian, for shits and giggles. <br /> <br /> You have a larceny charm for disguises. Does this apply all the way down to the genetic level? If someone were to take a brainscan or a genetic test of you, would they find any discrepancies? What about things like tattoos or embedded impants? In a world where everyone has an implant that has their ID number, does larceny take over it, or does it apply to craft? <br /> <br /> You are sent via transmission and resleeved into another body. Does the exaltation follow you? <br /> <br /> Do your resistance charms let you push away nanite swarms seeking to disassemble you? Do your parries defeat swarms of disassembler nanites? <br /> <br /> Congrats. You're now running a small system, and you're fighting against an alien empire. You have things like mass media, social networking, and TV. Let's say every morning your citizens wake up, go to the tv screen, and flip to the sports channel. Its transmitted live, and you guide your citizens through their morning exercises and mental training. Its a mix of tiger warrior training technique and legendary scholars curriculum. Does this work, Exalted excellence using technology to extend its reach? Or is this way too powerful?<br /> <br /> You carry out legendary scholar's curriclum, and log down your lectures and teachings in a video format. It is viewed later. Does it carry out the same absurd levels of increase in ability, or is the magic faded and they have to continuously rewind to understand what you're saying? <br /> <br /> You're a craft supernal, with some help in lore. And you can pull off some crazy shit. Someone chucks a laptop in front of you, and tell you to reverse-engineer, then improve it. Problem. You've only done things like make magic swords and things, since you're from a bronze age setting. Does this count as a legendary or superior project? Can you even do it? Does craftsman needs no tools let you obviate the need for clean rooms? <br /> <br /> Let's say that Exalted are in a Culture setting. Let's face it. They're going to fucking die when they fight against a Mind. Question is, how far does this go? Dawns can easily match the greatest of mortal generals in strategies, but what about a Culture Mind? Is there any power the Exalted that bring to bear that can ever match a Culture Mind, or are they hopelessly oumatched. Twilights can easily devise implants and upgrades and genetic alteration, but is it enough? Let's say that you have entire teams of dragonblooded Essence 5, in a warship, versus a Culture Mind. No effectors. Ship to ship battle. Skills in Sail, Archery, Stealth, and War. Is it a fight, or a stomp?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T03:44:50-07:00","id":1323408,"title":"","content":"Tattoos have been around for more than 5000 years. The concept of identification documents has been around for almost 3000 years if you count passports. I don\u2019t see why these would be too new for the Exalted to fake with their superlative skills.<br /> <br /> And if an Exalt in Creation can put together a fake \u201cthird arm mutation\u201d to pass himself off as someone, or fake the Emerald Thurible for his Mnemon costume from costume jewelry and paste, I don\u2019t see why someone from the Eclipse Phase setting couldn\u2019t make it look like they had a cybernetic arm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 07-10-2019, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T19:23:57-07:00","id":1323583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297140-exalted-meeting-alien-invasion?p=1297664#post1297664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh. Sorry.<br /> <br /> .... I thought the trauma part was hyperbole.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read it that way as well, jeesh the poster was only reminiscing of old forum flamewars. I highly doubt it was &quot;traumatic&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T21:37:31-07:00","id":1323608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297140-exalted-meeting-alien-invasion?p=1323397#post1323397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*thinks*<br /> <br /> So I've been wondering. Again. About things. Sorry if this gets repetitive, but I need some place to put my thoughts.<br /> <br /> <br /> Let's punt an Exaltation into Eclipse phase. Probably..... a Jovian, for shits and giggles.<br /> <br /> You have a larceny charm for disguises. Does this apply all the way down to the genetic level? If someone were to take a brainscan or a genetic test of you, would they find any discrepancies? What about things like tattoos or embedded impants? In a world where everyone has an implant that has their ID number, does larceny take over it, or does it apply to craft?<br /> <br /> You are sent via transmission and resleeved into another body. Does the exaltation follow you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The Exaltation is attached to the soul. Genetics--probably, as there's larceny to fake an anima banner. I see no reason for it not to. Brainscans likewise (although Socialize's persona charms might be more thorough).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297140-exalted-meeting-alien-invasion?p=1323397#post1323397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do your resistance charms let you push away nanite swarms seeking to disassemble you? Do your parries defeat swarms of disassembler nanites?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, as you can endure the Silent Wind of Hell and nuclear fires of Malfeas. Special angry bees aren't worse than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297140-exalted-meeting-alien-invasion?p=1323397#post1323397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Congrats. You're now running a small system, and you're fighting against an alien empire. You have things like mass media, social networking, and TV. Let's say every morning your citizens wake up, go to the tv screen, and flip to the sports channel. Its transmitted live, and you guide your citizens through their morning exercises and mental training. Its a mix of tiger warrior training technique and legendary scholars curriculum. Does this work, Exalted excellence using technology to extend its reach? Or is this way too powerful?<br /> <br /> You carry out legendary scholar's curriclum, and log down your lectures and teachings in a video format. It is viewed later. Does it carry out the same absurd levels of increase in ability, or is the magic faded and they have to continuously rewind to understand what you're saying?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it works as long as your alive, I think thats the standards for lingusitics (which seems fair to apply here).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297140-exalted-meeting-alien-invasion?p=1323397#post1323397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're a craft supernal, with some help in lore. And you can pull off some crazy shit. Someone chucks a laptop in front of you, and tell you to reverse-engineer, then improve it. Problem. You've only done things like make magic swords and things, since you're from a bronze age setting. Does this count as a legendary or superior project? Can you even do it? Does craftsman needs no tools let you obviate the need for clean rooms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on the Lore, probably superior (All Knowing Sage something lets you make lore checks on literally anything iirc).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297140-exalted-meeting-alien-invasion?p=1323397#post1323397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's say that Exalted are in a Culture setting. Let's face it. They're going to fucking die when they fight against a Mind. Question is, how far does this go? Dawns can easily match the greatest of mortal generals in strategies, but what about a Culture Mind? Is there any power the Exalted that bring to bear that can ever match a Culture Mind, or are they hopelessly oumatched. Twilights can easily devise implants and upgrades and genetic alteration, but is it enough? Let's say that you have entire teams of dragonblooded Essence 5, in a warship, versus a Culture Mind. No effectors. Ship to ship battle. Skills in Sail, Archery, Stealth, and War. Is it a fight, or a stomp?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no clue what a Culture Mind is, but I think the presumption of &quot;obviously Exalted lose&quot; is questionable. Someone else started an entire thread on this I think, I'd check that. I'd also go and check out the 2e shards that were scifi, both deal with exalted in highly technologically advanced settings (at least for a Lore perspective, not a mechanics one)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-10T22:21:01-07:00","id":1323613,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s not much difference between a Culture Mind and the Stellar Intelligences from <i>Shards of the Exalted Dream</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T06:01:09-07:00","id":1323655,"title":"","content":"Talking 2nd Ed, a Culture Mind is not beyond the scope of an Exalt.<br /> <br /> Looking at the attitude of Minds towards forces like Dra'Azon, you're not going to be able to convince me that they're beyond the scope of the Primordials... who had seven shades beaten out of them by the Exalted host. Hell, The Culture has regular, normal humans who are better at predicting events than Minds.<br /> <br /> A Idiran War Era Mind is Intelligence 7. A Modern Era (The State of The Art) is 8. A Late Culture (Surface Detail) is possibly up to 9 or 10 (they've clearly grown a pair when dealing with the Sublimed).<br /> <br /> It's not unthinkable that a Twilight or Dawn might beat a Mind at Gateway. It's like Reed Richards and Tony Stark playing chess. (Or Lex Luthor vs Superman. Or Superman vs The Flash. Man comic book characters love playing chess.)<br /> <br /> A Mind is on a par with a Third Circle Demon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297140-exalted-meeting-alien-invasion?p=1323608#post1323608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no clue what a Culture Mind is, but I think the presumption of &quot;obviously Exalted lose&quot; is questionable. Someone else started an entire thread on this I think, I'd check that. I'd also go and check out the 2e shards that were scifi, both deal with exalted in highly technologically advanced settings (at least for a Lore perspective, not a mechanics one)</div> </div> </div> </div>They're basically the smartest AIs in SciFi. They've &quot;solved&quot; science and created a Culture with unlimited energy and post scarcity production. Their proccessors are so large that they have to exist in hyperspace, in a quantum state (Marvin The Paranoid Android eat your heart out). Each Mind is grown from a unique seed AI and rewrites its own code, on the fly, for fun, so even if you could theoretically hack one that same technique wouldn't work on any other Mind.<br /> <br /> They can read minds. Predict the future. Maintain vast information networks that make the World Wide Web look like a toddler's story book. They treat with gods. And there's loads of them: an entire civilisation of them. Decked out with space ships with populations of billions and weapons that can annihilate... well... anything (unlimited energy supply, remember). They have resurrection technology and can make humans immortal. Masters of genetic engineering.<br /> <br /> A Mind is as far beyond a &quot;normal&quot; Exalt as an Essence 7+ Elder Exalt was above a normal Exalt in 2E.<br /> <br /> I think I AM is probably the only thing that comes close.<br /> <br /> But they don't have anything approximating Perfect effects. They do get out-fought and out-thought. Regular humans give them the slip or make better judgements or succeed where they fail. And a lot of that is luck (or a &quot;just as planned&quot; moment) but Minds aren't even the top dog in their setting and literally every book is about how some human nobody achieves something the Minds can't.<br /> <br /> The Culture is on the step above The Federation, hanging out with Time Lords, Darleks, Old Ones and Necrons.<br /> <br /> Spoiler for explaining The Grid<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Culture exists in a &quot;rocky road&quot; SciFi universe. It's soft-SciFi with hard Sci-Fi elements.<br /> <br /> A key conceit is that there exists a parallel anti-matter universe seperated from our universe by The Grid. Culture Minds can &quot;mine&quot; the Grid, either taking unlimited zero-point energy directly from the barrier between universes, or scooping up free abundant anti-matter. Spaceships can &quot;push off&quot; the Grid to enter hyperspace which runs more tangentially to reality than parallel, and the same hyperspace engines can make Dr Who style &quot;bigger on the inside&quot; feats of engineering (like the physical body of every single Mind). The Culture can also weaponise the Grid, intersplicing our universe with vast swarths of energy capable of reducing planets to rubble. And when that won't do they use Concetrated Anti-Matter weapons to utterly annihilate their targets. Man portable weapons include continent destroying nukes fired from pistols, monomolecular rocket powered intelligent knives and Concetrated Radiation Energy Weapon Systems (lasers). Their Special Circumstances footsoldiers are powered by anti-matter bombs.<br /> <br /> But they're not magic. They're constrained by physical laws. The Culture is a Super Power but it's not a Hyper Power.<br /> <br /> One Culture GSV is probably more powerful than Creation. Certainly the Culture has more impressive feats than the Exalted. But it's not a shocking difference. It's like Superman vs Goku. Superman is more powerful but it's not some trivial thing.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-11-2019, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T06:10:26-07:00","id":1323657,"title":"","content":"Woah. 8 or 7?<br /> <br /> A mind can literally simulate entire universes and more. Take control of an entire city. Do shit which would be insane even for high essence Exalted<br /> <br /> I would put them intelligent 10. At least","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T06:15:03-07:00","id":1323659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297140-exalted-meeting-alien-invasion?p=1323657#post1323657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mind can literally simulate entire universes and more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and an Intelligence <i>3</i> Solar can simulate an entire city out in the Wyld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T06:25:25-07:00","id":1323661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297140-exalted-meeting-alien-invasion?p=1297167#post1297167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>One arrow</i> doesn't incapacitate a ship, let alone a spaceship; it's gonna take a hell of a lot more than a simple Solar sniper build. Even a veritable hail of arrows only deals a single Hull level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there is that E5 solar archery charm... it even explicitly does extra hull damage. you can get to a dozen hull damage with proper initiative buildup.<br /> <br /> It will take more than what you said, but it's feasible. Three or four solars unopposed and properly built for that would create such scenario.<br /> <br /> Revamping those 50k people into about twice as many, nearly all trained to peak capacity and equipped would, in my opinion, still produce a comparatively small fleet, which ultimately gives &quot;the company&quot; an advantage in sheer scope. they'd still have to bet on the company not being willing to spend so damn much to get to that place.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T07:17:16-07:00","id":1323669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297140-exalted-meeting-alien-invasion?p=1323659#post1323659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and an Intelligence <i>3</i> Solar can simulate an entire city out in the Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would still put that down to wyld shenanigans, rather than any real hyperinelligence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T07:28:18-07:00","id":1323673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297140-exalted-meeting-alien-invasion?p=1323669#post1323669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would still put that down to wyld shenanigans, rather than any real hyperinelligence.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that the capacity to create a simulation is not solely limited to one's Intelligence score. Being able to create a sophisticated simulation does not necessitate an Intelligence greater than 5.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T07:34:40-07:00","id":1323675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297140-exalted-meeting-alien-invasion?p=1323669#post1323669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would still put that down to wyld shenanigans, rather than any real hyperinelligence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't. The Wyld is clay, it's the Solar's understanding of Lore which shapes it.<br /> <br /> Devil Tigers shape worlds within their souls. Controlling cities is not beyond the Solars.<br /> <br /> And again, I'd say look at the high end. The Culture is extremely careful about not peeving off Sublimed races. The Exalted picked up their tourches and pitch forks and went off to geld the Master of The Universe.<br /> <br /> Mr. Adequate is not more powerful than The Ebon Dragon.<br /> <br /> It's not like there's some massive gulf between Minds and the Sublimed. It's a lot like the dynamics between the Unquestionable in Exalted. And even the weakest Mind is right up there with the most powerful Exalts... like a 3CD.<br /> <br /> I think a Mind and The End of All Wisdom would be very firm friends.<br /> <br /> And again, I say look at the low end. The Contact predictor from Consider Phlebas (breaks her leg mountain climbing without an AG harness, forget her name) is an ordinary human who outthinks Minds. She's not going to be higher than Intelligence 6, yet routinely outthinks Minds. Look at the Chairmaker (*please don't discuss the enormous book ruining spoilers around the Chairmaker): granted there's normally a Mind in the background, smoothing things along for him, but in any kind of crossover event he's immediately getting a Night Caste Exaltation and he's made Minds look like laughing stocks as a regular (ish) mortal.<br /> <br /> A Culture Mind is way above human normal. That's what 7+ is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-11T08:36:44-07:00","id":1323694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1297140-exalted-meeting-alien-invasion?p=1323675#post1323675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Culture Mind is way above human normal. That's what 7+ is.</div> </div> </div> </div>5 is <i>also</i> &quot;way above human normal.&quot; It's somewhere between two to five times higher than &quot;human normal.&quot;<br /> <br /> But yeah, 7 seems reasonable. 10 does not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}